  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Crossborder emergency response in WASH and Protection to the crisis in Uvira</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An integrated WASH and Protection intervention for more than 48,000 people across Uvira territory in DRC and Bujumbura province in Burundi, with flexibility to adapt activities as transit sites shift. The program links safe water, sanitation, and hygiene promotion with GBV case management, psychosocial support, and child protection, ensuring 92% of beneficiaries receive services in both sectors. WASH activities include rehabilitating health facilities, installing latrines and water points, and conducting hygiene campaigns, while Protection interventions provide dignity kits, counseling, community centers, and referral pathways aligned with international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
