  <activity-status code="2"></activity-status>
  <activity-date iso-date="2025-12-24" type="2"></activity-date>
  <activity-date iso-date="2026-06-23" type="3"></activity-date>
  <recipient-country code="BI" percentage="100">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IRC will provide technical supervision of WASH interventions in Burundi to ensure coherence and alignment with SPHERE standards. IRC will conduct protection monitoring and security audits, and establish a community protection center (CPC) to welcome women and girls, including survivors, children, persons with disabilities, and child-friendly spaces (counseling office, recreational activities).The project will provide psychosocial support and case management sessions as well as recreational activities, and will identify and strengthen the capacities of community leaders and activists in legal assistance in matters related to protection.</narrative>
  </recipient-country>
  <recipient-country code="CD" percentage="100">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IRC will provide training for service providers, community health workers, and local hygiene committees on IPC, and will likewise build capacity in IPC awareness-raising techniques within these community structures, in collaboration with the Ministry of Health. Technical supervision of WASH interventions will be provided to ensure coherence and alignment with SPHERE and cluster standards. Technical supervision of Protection interventions through IRC&apos;s technical experts in DRC will also be provided.</narrative>
  </recipient-country>
